    "result": "## Summary\n\nThe bug has been successfully fixed! The issue was that the `frai` CLI's parent command had a `--ci` option defined, which was being parsed at the top level instead of being passed through to the `gate` subcommand.\n\n**Changes made to `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`:**\n\n1. **Line 604**: Added `.enablePositionalOptions()` to the main `frai` command - this allows positional options to be handled correctly\n2. **Line 741**: Replaced `.allowUnknownOption(true)` with `.passThroughOptions()` on the `gate` command - this ensures all options (including those defined on parent commands) are passed through to the delegated frai-gate CLI instead of being parsed by Commander.js\n\n**Verification:**\n- \u2705 Rebuilt the frai CLI with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n- \u2705 Tested `frai gate init --ci` in a clean directory\n- \u2705 Both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` are now created correctly",
